<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>Alignment - 标签 - lilfry's library</title><link>https://lilfry09.github.io/tags/alignment/</link><description>Alignment - 标签 - lilfry's library</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>zh-CN</language><managingEditor>lilfry@sjtu.edu.cn (lilfry)</managingEditor><webMaster>lilfry@sjtu.edu.cn (lilfry)</webMaster><copyright>All rights reserved.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:22:00 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://lilfry09.github.io/tags/alignment/" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>读 Selective DPO：偏好数据为什么不是越难越好</title><link>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/selective-dpo-data-difficulty/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:22:00 +0800</pubDate><author>fry</author><guid>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/selective-dpo-data-difficulty/</guid><description><![CDATA[<p>偏好对齐里有一个很自然的直觉：只要 chosen 和 rejected 没有标错，数据越多越好；难样本甚至应该更有训练价值。</p>
<p>Selective DPO 挑战了这个直觉。它提出，偏好数据是否有用，不只取决于标签质量，也取决于样本难度是否落在当前模型的能力范围内。</p>
<p>论文的核心主张是：</p>
<blockquote>
<p>偏好样本具有稳定的难度差异；过难样本会因为超过模型容量而伤害对齐，而且“过难”的阈值随模型能力变化。</p></blockquote>]]></description></item><item><title>面试高频：Bradley-Terry vs Plackett-Luce，奖励建模到底差在哪</title><link>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/bt-vs-pl-ranking-in-alignment/</link><pubDate>Wed, 08 Apr 2026 14:20:00 +0800</pubDate><author>fry</author><guid>https://lilfry09.github.io/ai/bt-vs-pl-ranking-in-alignment/</guid><description>一句话：BT 是 PL 在候选数 N=2 时的特例。BT 更轻、更稳、更适合现有 RLHF/DPO；PL 信息更全，但标注和训练成本显著更高。</description></item></channel></rss>